    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d644">

                <pb facs="0664" n="654" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg654"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/6–2749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-27T16:00:00+08:00">June 27, 1949—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 28—5:49 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 652. Note with text contained telCan 369, June 22 delivered Foreign Office
                    today. Foreign Office agreeable extension JCRR and <pb facs="0665" n="655"
                        xml:id="pg655"/> reply will be sent US tomorrow. Will telegraph when reply
                        received<anchor n="37" xml:id="d644-f1"/> and notes will go forward by
                        pouch.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d644-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d644-f1" n="37" xml:id="d644-f1-content">
                <p>Cantel No. 662, June 28, 6 p. m., not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d644-f2" n="38" xml:id="d644-f2-content">
                <p>Despatch No. 18, June 28, not printed; for texts of notes dated June 27, see
                    Department of State, Treaties and Other International Acts Series No. 1975; or
                    63 Stat. (pt. 3) 2702.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
